e>Kaplan</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>ProtoNet 4.0: a hierarchical classification of one million protein sequences</article-title><source>Nucleic Acids Res</source><year>2005</year><volume>33</volume><issue>(Database issue)</issue><fpage>D216</fpage><lpage>D218</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15608180</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B10"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kifer</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Predicting fold novelty based on ProtoNet hierarchical classification</article-title><source>Bioinformatics</source><year>2005</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>1020</fpage><lpage>1027</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15539447</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B11"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Krause</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Large scale hierarchical clustering of protein sequences</article-title><source>BMC Bioinformatics</source><year>2005</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>6</fpage><lpage>15</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15644130</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B12"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lazareva-Ulitsky</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>On the quality of tree-based protein classification</article-title><source>Bioinformatics</source><year>2005</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>1876</fpage><lpage>1890</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15647305</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B13"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Rost</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><artic